---
/**
 * Plan limits, one card per account, each with the badge the app puts on a reading:
 * where it came from and how old it is. The tick on each bar is the pace line.
 *
 * The copy is CHANGELOG.md's "Usage, per account": `get_usage` asked of the
 * account's own headless `claude`, the cache on disk as the fallback, and a
 * forecast that declines a reading too old to be sound.
 */
import { fillFor, LIMITS } from "../data/fleet";
import SectionCopy from "./SectionCopy.astro";
---

<section id="limits" class="scroll-mt-20 py-[96px]">
  <div class="wrap grid grid-cols-1 items-start gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-16">
    <SectionCopy
      eyebrow="Plan limits"
      heading="How much is left, per account, and when it comes back."
    >
      <p class="m-0 text-[16px] leading-[1.6] text-pretty text-fg-dim">
        The 5-hour and 7-day windows for every account, with reset times, a pace line and a
        forecast. Claude Code's are asked of the account's own <code>claude</code>, in a request
        that costs no tokens, with the cache on disk as the fallback. A badge says which one answered
        and how old the figure is, because a stale number that looks live is worse than none.
      </p>
      <p class="m-0 text-[14px] leading-[1.6] text-pretty text-fg-muted">
        Armada holds no vendor credentials. There is no sign-in, and nothing reads or stores a
        token: every account speaks for itself, through the CLI you already installed. Codex homes
        sit beside them, read from their session logs, with how old the figure is shown first. Grok
        Build writes its weekly allowance nowhere on disk, so Armada asks your own <code>grok</code>,
        the same question its <code>/usage</code> asks, and it costs nothing.
      </p>
    </SectionCopy>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      {
        LIMITS.map((l) => (
          <div class="reveal flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-[14px] border border-rule bg-bg-2 px-6 py-[22px]">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
              <span class="font-mono text-[13px] text-fg">{l.account}</span>
              <span
                class:list={[
                  "rounded-full border border-rule px-2.5 py-[3px] font-mono text-[10px]",
                  l.source === "live" ? "text-ok-ink" : "text-warn",
                ]}
              >
                {l.source} · {l.age}
              </span>
            </div>
            {l.windows.map((w) => (
              <div class="flex flex-col gap-[7px]">
                <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2.5">
                  <span class="text-[12.5px] text-fg-dim">
                    {w.label} <span class="text-fg">{w.used}%</span>
                  </span>
                  <span class="font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-muted">{w.reset}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="relative h-1.5 rounded-full bg-white/7">
                  <div
                    class:list={["bar", fillFor(w, l.source), l.source === "cache" && "opacity-60"]}
                    style={`width:${w.used}%`}
                  />
                  <span
                    class="absolute -top-[3px] block h-3 w-px bg-fg-dim"
                    style={`left:${w.pace}%`}
                    aria-hidden="true"
                  />
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        ))
      }
      <span class="font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-muted">
        Figures are examples · the tick is where an even pace would be by now
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
